config VIDEO_OV9281
	tristate "OmniVision OV9281 sensor support (NOT for the Chronos board)"
	depends on I2C && VIDEO_DEV
	select MEDIA_CONTROLLER
	select VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
	select V4L2_FWNODE
	help
	  This is a V4L2 sensor driver for the OmniVision OV9281
	  global shutter camera sensor, for setups where the sensor is
	  directly attached to the host's I2C bus and MIPI receiver.

	  DO NOT enable or load this driver on the Chronos board
	  (HW_CHRONOS_R1): there the OV9281 sensors live on FPGA-private
	  SCCB buses that the Jetson cannot reach, and the FPGA owns the
	  complete sensor configuration (27 MHz XCLK, FSIN trigger mode,
	  30 fps).  This driver's 24 MHz / 120 fps free-run defaults
	  conflict with that.  Use CHRONOS_FPGA and VIDEO_CHRONOS_CSI
	  instead.  It is kept only as a reference for a future hardware
	  revision.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
	  module will be called ov9281.
